# Who Am I

**Almudena "Almu" Vivanco**

Principal Performance Engineer, Chaos Engineering advocate, and international speaker focused on performance, observability, resilience, and cloud-native platforms.

With more than 20 years of experience building and testing large-scale distributed systems, Almu helps organizations move beyond traditional testing and adopt resilience engineering practices that prepare systems for real-world failures.

## What I Believe In

- Treating failure as a feature, not something to avoid
- Making resilience testing part of automated delivery pipelines
- Defining chaos experiments as code and versioning them like software
- Using observability and SLOs to verify system behavior under stress

## What I Teach

- How to use Chaos Mesh on Kubernetes
- How to drive experiments from k6 and xk6-kubernetes
- How to automate Chaos Engineering workflows
- How to validate resilience using automated assertions
- How to integrate resilience testing into delivery pipelines

## In This Workshop

This repository and session are designed to show how modern cloud-native systems can be tested not only for performance, but also for resilience under failure.

The goal is to help teams learn from experiments that intentionally break systems, so they can build more reliable systems with confidence.

